<title>USA: Five bidders for U.S. Stockpile spot tin.</title>
<headline>Five bidders for U.S. Stockpile spot tin.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five companies presented bids for U.S. Stockpile tin sold monthly on a sealed bid, spot basis.</p>
<p>American Iron and Metal bid for 80 tonnes at $2.509 to $2.5136 per lb, Allied Deals bid for 40 tonnes at $2.5267, Rotometals bid for five tonnes at $2.52, Baron Metals and Alloys bid for 60 tonnes at $2.517, and Ney Smelting bid for 20 tonnes at $2.5261.</p>
<p>The outcome is due soon.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
